 "debrief": "In Josephus’s account, Cestius suddenly broke off the siege of Jerusalem, perhaps fearing winter or supply, and retreated. In the narrow pass of Beth Horon the rebels attacked from the heights. He killed his mules and abandoned engines, left 400 men behind to fool the rebels and fled by night. About 6,000 Romans died, and the Twelfth Legion’s eagle was lost. Nero then sent Vespasian to Judaea. The other choices are what-ifs.",
